    "difficulty": "hard",
    "item_data_json": "{\"options\":{\"A\":\"Explain that unit routine takes precedence over cultural or religious requests after death because consistent workflow is necessary for equitable treatment of all families on the unit.\",\"B\":\"Clarify what the client and family specifically want, document those preferences, and coordinate reasonable accommodations that are safe and consistent with law and facility policy.\",\"C\":\"Assume the request represents the standard practice of everyone from the same cultural group and apply the same ritual automatically to other clients from that background.\",\"D\":\"Delay discussion until after death because discussing rituals in advance may increase distress and does not contribute meaningfully to individualized end-of-life planning.\"}}",
